<p>A Udemy side hustle is the closest thing to "record once, get paid for years" that most people can actually pull off. You build a video course about something you already know, upload it to a marketplace with tens of millions of learners, and Udemy handles the hosting, payments, refunds and most of the marketing. The catch is that Udemy keeps a big slice of each sale, prices are discounted constantly, and a single course rarely pays the rent.</p>
<p>This guide walks through exactly how Udemy instructor payment works as of 2026, what the platform requires before you can charge for a course, how to pick a topic that sells, and what income to realistically expect. If you are still deciding whether teaching online is your thing at all, the <a href="/tools/side-hustle-quiz/">side hustle quiz</a> is a fast sanity check.</p>

