<h2 id="affiliate">The Udemy affiliate program</h2>
<p>You do not have to teach to earn from Udemy. The <a href="https://www.udemy.com/affiliate/">Udemy affiliate program</a> runs mainly through the Impact network and pays a commission on courses bought through your links. Udemy's partner help pages describe a baseline commission of roughly 10–15% (they list both figures in different places) and a 7-day cookie, and a purchase of any course within that window counts. Commissions on refunded sales are reversed.</p>
<p>A 7-day cookie is short, so this works best for bloggers and YouTubers who recommend specific courses to readers who are ready to buy. Project your numbers with the <a href="/tools/affiliate-commission-calculator/">affiliate commission calculator</a>.</p>

<h2 id="mistakes">Common Udemy mistakes to avoid</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Making the course too long.</strong> A focused three-hour course that delivers one clear result usually gets better reviews than a bloated 20-hour one that students never finish.</li>
  <li><strong>Skipping the promo video.</strong> It is often the first thing a buyer watches. Show your face, state the outcome and keep it short.</li>
  <li><strong>Ignoring Q&amp;A.</strong> Slow or missing answers lead to bad reviews, and reviews drive Udemy's search ranking.</li>
  <li><strong>Publishing one course and waiting.</strong> Income usually compounds across a catalog, because students who like one course buy the next.</li>
  <li><strong>Forgetting quarterly taxes.</strong> Udemy does not withhold tax for US instructors, so track your earnings from the first payout.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom line</h2>
<p>A Udemy side hustle is a good fit if you have a practical, in-demand skill and would rather spend time teaching than building a website and running ads. Go in expecting a slow start, build more than one course in the same niche, and push your own students through coupon links to earn the 97% share. If you would rather keep more of each sale and own your student list, compare <a href="/thinkific/">Thinkific</a>, and browse more ideas on the <a href="/blog/">Better Side Hustles blog</a>.</p>
